  rankdir="TB";
  "N1" [label="(1,0,0) Spinons are well-established in 1D systems"];
  "N10" [label="(7,0,0) Spin-orbit-entangled pseudospin-1/2 square-lattice AFs in iridates offer novel platforms in uncharted parameter regime"];
  "N11" [label="(8,0,0) Strong spin-orbit coupling in iridates imparts unique properties to exchange interactions"];
  "N13" [label="(10,0,0) SL Sr2IrO4 shows strong deviation from NN Heisenberg model"];
  "N15" [label="(11,0,0) Nature of exchange interactions varies widely within R-P series iridates"];
  "N17" [label="(12,1,0) Heterointerfacing may induce magnetic frustration through proximity coupling of symmetry-distinct orders"];
  "N19" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction-rule: If experimental evidence shows isotropic continua dominating spectra instead of magnons, then spinons exist in the system"];
  "N2" [label="(1,1,0) Spinons in dimensions >1D remain contentious"];
  "N27" [label="(13,0,0) Proposal component: Demonstrate heterostructure-based strategy to frustrate Néel AF order in square-lattice iridates"];
  "N30" [label="(16,0,0) Proposal component: Observe isotropic continua as evidence for spinons"];
  "N4" [label="(3,0,0) Despite Néel AF orders and no apparent frustrations, these systems can accommodate gapped spinon modes"];
  "N5" [label="(4,0,0) Broad continua '(π,0) anomaly' in copper-based square-lattice AFs attributed to spinon excitations"];
  "N8" [label="(6,0,0) Parameters affecting spinon weights are difficult to control experimentally"];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) Investigate whether heterointerfacing distinct Ruddlesden-Popper iridates can engineer magnetic frustration in square-lattice antiferromagnets and thereby enable time-resolved RXD and polarization-resolved RIXS tests for possible deconfined spinon excitations, using signatures such as suppressed single-magnon modes and isotropic continua.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) When higher-dimensional spinon physics is unsettled but theoretically and spectroscopically motivated, a controllable material platform that can tune magnetic frustration and a measurement strategy sensitive to continua versus magnons together define a testable experimental research program."];
  "R1" [label="(0,0,0) Spinons are established in one-dimensional systems, while their status in dimensions greater than one remains scientifically contentious."];
  "R10" [label="(0,0,0) Because spinons beyond one dimension remain contentious and parameters affecting spinon weights are difficult to control experimentally, new material platforms with more controllable parameters are motivated for studying spinons."];
  "R11" [label="(0,0,0) Spin-orbit-entangled pseudospin-1/2 square-lattice antiferromagnets in iridates provide novel platforms with distinctive exchange-interaction properties."];
  "R12" [label="(0,0,0) The variation of exchange interactions across Ruddlesden-Popper iridates, together with the possibility that heterointerfacing induces magnetic frustration through proximity coupling of symmetry-distinct orders, motivates using iridate heterostructures as a route to engineered magnetic frustration."];
  "R13" [label="(0,0,0) The possibility of spinon-like excitations in two-dimensional square lattices, together with the need for more controllable material platforms, motivates developing new platforms for experimental spinon studies."];
  "R2" [label="(0,0,0) Within Ruddlesden-Popper iridates, different compounds exhibit substantially different exchange-interaction behavior, including strong deviation from the nearest-neighbor Heisenberg model in Sr2IrO4 and an exceptionally large spin gap in Sr3Ir2O7."];
  "R6" [label="(0,0,0) If measurements show isotropic continua dominating spectra rather than conventional magnon modes, those spectra would support interpreting the excitations as spinons."];
  "R7" [label="(0,0,0) A coherent research program is to use iridate heterostructures to frustrate Néel antiferromagnetic order in square-lattice systems and evaluate possible spinon physics with time-resolved RXD and polarization-resolved RIXS signatures such as suppressed single magnons and isotropic continua."];
  "R8" [label="(0,0,0) Copper-based square-lattice antiferromagnets and Néel-ordered square-lattice systems motivate the possibility that two-dimensional square lattices can accommodate spinon-like excitations."];
  "N1" -> "R1" [label="induction-case"];
